# What never reaches the build context (SHIP-187).
#
# The context is services/core rather than the repository root, which already puts deploy/.env,
# the Flutter app and node_modules out of reach — see the header of Dockerfile for why that is a
# security property and not a convenience. What is left to exclude is noise: files that change on
# every run, invalidate the COPY layer, and are never read by a build.
#
# A build that ignores nothing still produces a correct image. It produces it slower, and it puts
# a developer's local build output into a layer, which is how a stale binary ends up shipped
# beside a fresh one.

# Test binaries and coverage output, per the root .gitignore's Go section.
*.test
*.out
coverage.*

# A bare `go build ./cmd/<name>` run from services/core drops the binary here rather than into
# bin/. The root .gitignore lists these one per command for the reason given there; the same list
# applies for the same reason.
/api
/lintboundaries
/migrate
/notifier
/statusgen
/topics
/worker

# Nothing in the image build reads a test, and the integration tests are the bulk of the tree.
# They are excluded from the context, not from the build: `make check` on the host is what runs
# them, and CI runs that before an image is ever built.
**/*_test.go
**/testdata/

# The build stage runs `go mod download` against go.mod and go.sum. A vendor directory in the
# context would be copied and then ignored, which is the slowest possible way to reach the same
# result.
/vendor/

# Editor and OS leftovers.
.DS_Store
*.swp
